  "query_preview": "..\nNext 7 days (Through Saturday)...\n\nThere is a moderate chance for frost through early this morning \nfor locations along the foothills and the higher hills over \nsoutheast Montana.\n\nConditions will trend drier into Tuesday, outside of occasional \npieces of energy bringing isolated shower and weak thunderstorm \nactivity to the mountains and far east in the afternoons and \nevenings. Monday may see breezy conditions near the Dakota border,\nwith a 20-40% chance for gusts up to 35 mph. Late Tuesday into \nWednesday, a stronger wave is expected to impact the region, \nbringing a better chance (30-60%) for showers and thunderstorms \nas well as breezy winds (gusts 30 to 45 mph) over the foothills \nTuesday and over the east Wednesday.\n\nThrough the end of the work week, occasional pieces of energy \nwill continue to move through the flow, allowing isolated \nafternoon and evening showers and thunderstorms to continue. \nHeading into the weekend, there are hints that upper troughing \nmoves onto the West Coast, inducing southwest flow over the \nregion, with a better potential for daily thunderstorms.\n\nHighs today will be in the 60s to low 70s, increasing to mostly\n80s by Tuesday. Into the weekend, temperatures look to decrease\ninto the 70s to low 80s. Archer",
